      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Difficult airway management in the gravid patient is a well-described phenomenon. We present a case of emergent cesarean delivery complicated by a \"cannot intubate, cannot ventilate\" scenario that was later determined to be secondary to an allergic, IgE-mediated reaction to epidurally administered local anesthetic."},
